  "rationale": "The first and finest of Booker Ervin's celebrated 'Book' series for Prestige, The Freedom Book is his defining statement as a leader \u2014 a session that captures his tough Texas tenor at its most focused and lyrical. The quartet of Ervin, Jaki Byard, Richard Davis, and Alan Dawson operates as a genuine ensemble, not a blowing date; Byard's pianistic wit and Davis/Dawson's telepathic rhythm section push Ervin into some of his most adventurous yet grounded playing. AllMusic (4.5\u2605), Rolling Stone Jazz Record Guide (5\u2605), and Penguin Guide (4\u2605) all mark it as essential. Ervin is absent from the canon entirely; this is the record that belongs.",
